{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1200835-does-the-half-life-merit-really-turn-you-into-a-vampire-wraith-hybrid","id":1200835,"title":"Does the Half-Life Merit really turn you into a Vampire/Wraith hybrid?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Vampire: The Masquerade"],"posts":[{"date":"2018-03-29T09:19:28-07:00","id":1200835,"title":"Does the Half-Life Merit really turn you into a Vampire/Wraith hybrid?","content":"The Half-Life Merit from Lore of the Bloodlines (p.48) starts as follows:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lore of the Bloodlines</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\"><b>Half-Life (6pt. Merit)</b><br /> <br /> You\u2019re more than just a vampire; you\u2019re a wraith in vampire form.</div> </div> </div> </div>Simply put, that seems way too powerful. Just like that you can be a Vampire/Wraith hybrid, access to Arcanoi like you're a Wraith and all other powers, but still have the strengths and weaknesses of a vampire. It might be that this Merit was not intended this way, but going by the wording it does suggest that taking it lets you be a Vampire/Wraith hybrid. Did I miss anything, or is this really how this Merit was intended?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12085-beriorn","name":"Beriorn","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12085_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-29T10:38:14-07:00","id":1200865,"title":"","content":"It was a merit introduced to explain a fun little concept to play with for the Harbingers. It was also introduced with the idea likely that you could flat out ignore it because you don't like the implications. But I would rule it you don't have Arcanoi while in a physical body, but it would be interesting to make say your Astral form more Wraithlike.<br /> <br /> Hell it would be a cool Necromancy/Auspex Combo that allowed your Astral Form to Learn Arcanoi. Sort of a simpler basic version of what Cappy did.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/754-eldagusto","name":"Eldagusto","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar754_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-29T10:46:35-07:00","id":1200872,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Beriorn</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1200835-does-the-half-life-merit-really-turn-you-into-a-vampire-wraith-hybrid#post1200835\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Half-Life Merit from Lore of the Bloodlines (p.48) starts as follows:<br /> <br /> <br /> Simply put, that seems way too powerful. Just like that you can be a Vampire/Wraith hybrid, access to Arcanoi like you're a Wraith and all other powers, but still have the strengths and weaknesses of a vampire. It might be that this Merit was not intended this way, but going by the wording it does suggest that taking it lets you be a Vampire/Wraith hybrid. Did I miss anything, or is this really how this Merit was intended?</div> </div> </div> </div>Nowhere in the merit's wording does it say anything about learning Arcanoi or having any wraith powers. You don't have lifesight, you don't have deathsight, you don't have Pathos, passions, relics, etc. All you get from Half-Life is a massive Necromancy discount and the ability to travel to the underworld.<br /> <br /> But I agree that this is one of the worst written merits out there. It just drops &quot;you are a half-ghost&quot; like it's the most natural thing out there. How did that happen? Why do other vampires hate you? Apparently they do, according to the merit, but why? How do they even recognize you? What a half-ghost's aura looks like can't be normal Auspex knowledge. It's a 6 point merit, it's incredibly rare. And if being recognized as a half-ghost is easy and is a death sentence, then why is this a 6 point merit and not a 6 point flaw?<br /> <br /> It's a bad merit, but it's not bad for the reasons you are mentioning.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12892-kammerer","name":"Kammerer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12892_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1191"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-29T10:56:45-07:00","id":1200878,"title":"","content":"I consider merits so out there with a different lens. I see them as originally written for NPCs, but they just included them as a why not for non standard games. Like most games won't allow it, but some may allow it because either everyone is a Harbinger with it or you are some sort of Storyteller's secret plot character.<br /> <br /> I mean before the 20th ed I was very much under the assumption I would probably ignore most merits. But with V20 and making Languages a Merit, which is silly because they are an essential character trait, that opened up Pandora's Box and forcibly made merits essential...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/754-eldagusto","name":"Eldagusto","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar754_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-29T12:02:37-07:00","id":1200911,"title":"","content":"That's a pretty bizarre idea. This merit is entirely meaningless as an NPC-only merit since NPCs don't track XP and ST can always just say that NPC necromancer also has Path of Ash in addition to every other path she has.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12892-kammerer","name":"Kammerer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12892_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1191"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-29T12:15:24-07:00","id":1200921,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kammerer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1200835-does-the-half-life-merit-really-turn-you-into-a-vampire-wraith-hybrid?p=1200911#post1200911\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That's a pretty bizarre idea. This merit is entirely meaningless as an NPC-only merit since NPCs don't track XP and ST can always just say that NPC necromancer also has Path of Ash in addition to every other path she has.</div> </div> </div> </div>I mean as an NPC merit only in that it points out they exist. As a placeholder saying these wonky ghost vamps are a thing.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/754-eldagusto","name":"Eldagusto","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar754_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-29T15:49:49-07:00","id":1201030,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Eldagusto</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1200835-does-the-half-life-merit-really-turn-you-into-a-vampire-wraith-hybrid?p=1200878#post1200878\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I before the 20th ed I was very much under the assumption I would probably ignore most merits. But with V20 and making Languages a Merit, which is silly because they are an essential character trait, that opened up Pandora's Box and forcibly made merits essential...</div> </div> </div> </div>Or just ignore the silly Languages merit, which doesn't work better than Linguistics skills. I'm thinking about adapting the Linguistic-skills (as well as Computers, and several others), sort of: if you're a 16th century scholar, one point in language will give you latin &amp; greek for free ; on the other hand, if you're 20th century &amp; non-native English speaker, one point will give you English (if you wish so), or another language; 2 would, I don't know, perhaps give you English for free, plus additionnal languages, etc., and maybe a familiarity with a related-languages. On the other hand, a 21st century vamp wouldn't need Computers 1 to use Internet ; a 16th century v would definitely need it. <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23992-tazmaniacs","name":"Tazmaniacs","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"46"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-29T15:56:14-07:00","id":1201032,"title":"","content":"I viewed language Personally as a Background could works well.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/754-eldagusto","name":"Eldagusto","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar754_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-30T01:04:30-07:00","id":1201180,"title":"","content":"As stated earlier, this Merit doesn't imply in the least that the character can learn Arcanoi, have the benefits of Lifesight or Deathsight, or any other aspect of the Wraith condition. If that had been the intent, the designers would have spelled that out directly in the Merit itself, as they spelled out the mechanics being a Ghoul over in Mage.<br /> <br /> <br /> This, however, is not why I'm here. I'm here to ask: If the Merit DID allow the Vampire to learn Arcanoi, would be actually be overpowered, as the original poster said?<br /> <br /> I don't think so. Setting aside for a moment that many Arcanoi may not even be applicable for a Vampire (I'm not familiar enough with Wraith to say either way). Or how of all the powers available to the Vampires, I can't imagine any Arcanoi would be very much more powerful than some of the Disciplines VtM has created over the years. Let's not even mention these points.<br /> <br /> Instead, here's this. There's a school of thought that says if you give one supernatural creature access to two different sets of powers, that also means the character must DIVIDE their experience points between the two powers. Even if the breadth of abilities a character could access is huge, their ability to learn and improve them is finite. If continuing to gain new and different powers is, in and of itself, inherently OP, then what makes a Vampire learning Arcanoi qualitatively different than learning out-of-clan Disciplines? Or blood sorcery, with its many Paths and Rituals?<br /> <br /> All for powers that are, at least in theory, as good as powers they gain natively, if dot ranks are anything to go by?<br /> <br /> The only possible exception to this tends to be Mage Spheres, since their applications are open-ended and flexible in a way other supernatural powers aren't. But even then, you're also investing large amounts of experience into those Spheres, AND into Arete, AND into any number of mundane Abilities that the character's Focus may rely upon to channel Effects. AND the use of those Sphere powers is subject to Paradox, which puts a ceiling on the kinds of things our hypothetical cross-trained supernatural creature can use &quot;safely&quot;.<br /> <br /> Not to mention, whether you're a different splat branching INTO Spheres or a Mage branching OUT, many of the powers gained (that you just spent a bunch of experience unlocking) will be redundant to powers you already have. But I digress.<br /> <br /> <br /> My point is, while I'd personally be reluctant to allow different splats free rein to learn each others' powers, I'm skeptical that allowing it would really break the game. On paper, letting Vampires learn Arcanoi SOUNDS overpowered. But in practice, the character is, at best, edging out advantages at unexpected angles, at the cost of failing to refine the greatest of their own native powers. Not useless, no, but neither is it a path to overwhelming power.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://archiveofourown.org/works/6956863/chapters/15862327\" target=\"_blank\">Magestuck: The Ascension</a></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6156-bluecho","name":"Bluecho","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3871"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-30T01:09:58-07:00","id":1201181,"title":"","content":"The Lore of the ... books anyway made Necromancy overpowered.<br /> With Lore of the Clans you get have a Merit (Mortuario) , a Background (Memento de Morte) and a Livel 1 Ritual (Death\u2019s Communion), that will give you when combined +7 dice and difficulty -2 on all Necromancy rolls. Throw Half-Live in the mix and and it becomes completely over powered.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5199-aahz","name":"Aahz","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"610"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-30T03:00:24-07:00","id":1201193,"title":"","content":"Personally, I just house ruled the merit as a XP discount on Fortitude, -2 difficulties on rolls when using a crowbar and muscle cars, at the cost of being hunted by the government. Also while you can sire childer, they're guaranteed to have infertile blood. OP really needs to not publish merits that can have unforeseen consequences.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/431-theodrim","name":"Theodrim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar431_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1841"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-30T04:31:05-07:00","id":1201206,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Theodrim</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1200835-does-the-half-life-merit-really-turn-you-into-a-vampire-wraith-hybrid?p=1201193#post1201193\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Personally, I just house ruled the merit as a XP discount on Fortitude, -2 difficulties on rolls when using a crowbar and muscle cars, at the cost of being hunted by the government. Also while you can sire childer, they're guaranteed to have infertile blood. OP really needs to not publish merits that can have unforeseen consequences.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well as written the merit has no unforseen consequences. It's weird and it raises more questions than it answers, but it has no consequences. Except that vampires are apparently racist against people with different aura color.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12892-kammerer","name":"Kammerer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12892_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1191"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-30T10:38:22-07:00","id":1201318,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kammerer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1200835-does-the-half-life-merit-really-turn-you-into-a-vampire-wraith-hybrid?p=1200872#post1200872\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Nowhere in the merit's wording does it say anything about learning Arcanoi or having any wraith powers. You don't have lifesight, you don't have deathsight, you don't have Pathos, passions, relics, etc. All you get from Half-Life is a massive Necromancy discount and the ability to travel to the underworld.<br /> <br /> But I agree that this is one of the worst written merits out there. It just drops &quot;you are a half-ghost&quot; like it's the most natural thing out there. How did that happen? Why do other vampires hate you? Apparently they do, according to the merit, but why? How do they even recognize you? What a half-ghost's aura looks like can't be normal Auspex knowledge. It's a 6 point merit, it's incredibly rare. And if being recognized as a half-ghost is easy and is a death sentence, then why is this a 6 point merit and not a 6 point flaw?<br /> <br /> It's a bad merit, but it's not bad for the reasons you are mentioning.</div> </div> </div> </div>It explains all of this fully if you read the chapter.<br /> <br /> The book exposes a new idea in the fluff; if a Vampire spends many years in the Underworld, there is damage to their soul, and risk of them simply being possessed by powerful and ancient wraiths. Personally I think it's a neat idea. If the Harbingers have hidden in the Shadowlands, often in Torpor, for centuries, then this should come with risks and downsides. Kindred are difficult to possess and control, but not impossible. Mechanically it's neat, if expensive.<br /> <br /> Other kindred don't know that your soul is secretly a wraith. It's a deeply-kept secret, and the merit actually mentions this. Just don't tell the Vampires you're infiltrating that you're an infiltrator?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11620-twig","name":"twig","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11620_5.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4568"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-30T10:40:17-07:00","id":1201319,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aahz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1200835-does-the-half-life-merit-really-turn-you-into-a-vampire-wraith-hybrid?p=1201181#post1201181\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Lore of the ... books anyway made Necromancy overpowered.<br /> With Lore of the Clans you get have a Merit (Mortuario) , a Background (Memento de Morte) and a Livel 1 Ritual (Death\u2019s Communion), that will give you when combined +7 dice and difficulty -2 on all Necromancy rolls. Throw Half-Live in the mix and and it becomes completely over powered.</div> </div> </div> </div>Except to have Half-Life you need to be a Cainite who has spent a long time in the Shadowlands, and to be a Mortuario you need to have undergone a ritual only the premascine Giovanni (those who were embraced before the Cappadocian betrayal) have.<br /> <br /> Yes it is entirely mechanically plausible to be a Mortuario Harbinger with Half-Life, but no ST is going to okay that. Furthermore, you've wasted the vast majority of your freebies, so you are EXTREMELY GOOD at the 1-3 dots of one path of Necromancy you have.<br /> <br /> These two merits require a deeply contorted backstory which no one will okay. I died accidentally, and a Harbinger and a Premascine worked together to bring me back, and then kicked me into torpor in the shadowlands for 100 years... NO! I am NOT powergaming!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11620-twig","name":"twig","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11620_5.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4568"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-30T10:44:24-07:00","id":1201321,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Bluecho</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1200835-does-the-half-life-merit-really-turn-you-into-a-vampire-wraith-hybrid?p=1201180#post1201180\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">As stated earlier, this Merit doesn't imply in the least that the character can learn Arcanoi, have the benefits of Lifesight or Deathsight, or any other aspect of the Wraith condition. If that had been the intent, the designers would have spelled that out directly in the Merit itself, as they spelled out the mechanics being a Ghoul over in Mage.<br /> <br /> <br /> This, however, is not why I'm here. I'm here to ask: If the Merit DID allow the Vampire to learn Arcanoi, would be actually be overpowered, as the original poster said?<br /> <br /> I don't think so. Setting aside for a moment that many Arcanoi may not even be applicable for a Vampire (I'm not familiar enough with Wraith to say either way). Or how of all the powers available to the Vampires, I can't imagine any Arcanoi would be very much more powerful than some of the Disciplines VtM has created over the years. Let's not even mention these points.<br /> <br /> Instead, here's this. There's a school of thought that says if you give one supernatural creature access to two different sets of powers, that also means the character must DIVIDE their experience points between the two powers. Even if the breadth of abilities a character could access is huge, their ability to learn and improve them is finite. If continuing to gain new and different powers is, in and of itself, inherently OP, then what makes a Vampire learning Arcanoi qualitatively different than learning out-of-clan Disciplines? Or blood sorcery, with its many Paths and Rituals?<br /> <br /> All for powers that are, at least in theory, as good as powers they gain natively, if dot ranks are anything to go by?<br /> <br /> The only possible exception to this tends to be Mage Spheres, since their applications are open-ended and flexible in a way other supernatural powers aren't. But even then, you're also investing large amounts of experience into those Spheres, AND into Arete, AND into any number of mundane Abilities that the character's Focus may rely upon to channel Effects. AND the use of those Sphere powers is subject to Paradox, which puts a ceiling on the kinds of things our hypothetical cross-trained supernatural creature can use &quot;safely&quot;.<br /> <br /> Not to mention, whether you're a different splat branching INTO Spheres or a Mage branching OUT, many of the powers gained (that you just spent a bunch of experience unlocking) will be redundant to powers you already have. But I digress.<br /> <br /> <br /> My point is, while I'd personally be reluctant to allow different splats free rein to learn each others' powers, I'm skeptical that allowing it would really break the game. On paper, letting Vampires learn Arcanoi SOUNDS overpowered. But in practice, the character is, at best, edging out advantages at unexpected angles, at the cost of failing to refine the greatest of their own native powers. Not useless, no, but neither is it a path to overwhelming power.</div> </div> </div> </div>Fully agreed. WtA and Mage talk about this.<br /> <br /> If giving a Werewolf Sorcery, which they have to buy with Freebies and EXP, you have to remember that every point going into that is a point not going into Gifts, Attributes, Abilities etc.<br /> <br /> If a Mage is learning Sorcery, they are getting paradox-free &quot;magic&quot; which they can use in a pinch (now the book also says you can simply say that Mages need to use Magick and can't use linear powers). It's powerful and useful! But it's not &quot;OP&quot; as they could be bumping up Arete or Spheres.<br /> <br /> Now, if you were dealing with an ancient Harbinger with Arcanoi and Necromancy basically mastered, then that would be a terrifying villain/NPC, but their power is a matter of ST caveat, not PC rules and creation systems.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11620-twig","name":"twig","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11620_5.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4568"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-30T11:37:43-07:00","id":1201342,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>11twiggins</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1200835-does-the-half-life-merit-really-turn-you-into-a-vampire-wraith-hybrid?p=1201318#post1201318\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> It explains all of this fully if you read the chapter.</div> </div> </div> </div>Weird how I don't see any such requirement in the merit description.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12892-kammerer","name":"Kammerer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12892_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1191"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-30T11:59:20-07:00","id":1201348,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kammerer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1200835-does-the-half-life-merit-really-turn-you-into-a-vampire-wraith-hybrid?p=1201342#post1201342\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Weird how I don't see any such requirement in the merit description.</div> </div> </div> </div>...really are we going this route?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/754-eldagusto","name":"Eldagusto","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar754_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-30T12:17:36-07:00","id":1201357,"title":"","content":"I don't consider the Merit overpowered at all.<br /> <br /> But I wrote it, so I would say that <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><span style=\"color:#000080\">Matthew Dawkins</span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000080\">In-House Developer for Onyx Path Publishing</span></b><br /> <br /> <i><span style=\"font-family:arial\"><b><span style=\"color:#008080\">Website: </span><a href=\"http://www.matthewdawkins.com\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008080\">https://www.matthewdawkins.com</span></a><br /> <span style=\"color:#008080\">Patreon: </span><a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/matthewdawkins\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008080\">https://www.patreon.com/matthewdawkins</span></a></b></span></i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/152-the-gentleman-gamer","name":"The Gentleman Gamer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar152_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1698"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-30T12:47:09-07:00","id":1201364,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kammerer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1200835-does-the-half-life-merit-really-turn-you-into-a-vampire-wraith-hybrid?p=1201342#post1201342\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Weird how I don't see any such requirement in the merit description.</div> </div> </div> </div>If you read the chapter for the Harbingers in LotB, rather than jumping to the merits (which require context), and refuse to read up on the proceeding lore, then the merit is incomplete and doesn't fully explain itself. But it's a really complex situation and the word-count is very limited. Having just spent quite a few words explaining the Half-Life state throughout the chapter (including a big scary reveal that most of the inner circle of Harbingers are servants of an extremely powerful Wraith, and have been compromised by wraithly possession themselves), I can see why <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/152-the-gentleman-gamer\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar152_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"152\" data-vbnamecard=\"152\">The Gentleman Gamer</a> didn't decide to hold the hands of people who hadn't read the whole chapter by giving a full in-depth explanation AGAIN.<br /> <br /> The merit is relatively balanced considering how expensive it is, and how its EXP saving effect only applies to buying secondary paths beyond the first dot. It will save you a lot of EXP in the long run, if you are playing a Necromancer who wants to master every Path available to them. The simple means of crossing from Skin to Shadowlands is extremely useful, and means you don't need to master Ash to function on both sides (although the path would still be very useful). As for the lore behind it, maybe read the chapter before acting like an authority on one of its merits? Will save you a lot of grief.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":11620,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11620-twig","user":"twig","date":". 03-30-2018, 03:50 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11620-twig","name":"twig","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11620_5.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4568"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-30T12:59:39-07:00","id":1201367,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Eldagusto</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1200835-does-the-half-life-merit-really-turn-you-into-a-vampire-wraith-hybrid?p=1201348#post1201348\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">...really are we going this route?</div> </div> </div> </div>Is there a Flaw where a PC picks dumb hills to die on? <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11620-twig","name":"twig","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11620_5.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4568"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-30T13:02:40-07:00","id":1201372,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Gentleman Gamer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1200835-does-the-half-life-merit-really-turn-you-into-a-vampire-wraith-hybrid?p=1201357#post1201357\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I don't consider the Merit overpowered at all.<br /> <br /> But I wrote it, so I would say that <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>I mean a merit in the proceeding &quot;Lore Of&quot; book reduces all Necromancy roll difficulties by 2 in exchange for some manageable weaknesses, so it would struggle to be OP in that context.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11620-twig","name":"twig","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11620_5.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4568"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-30T14:06:51-07:00","id":1201407,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Gentleman Gamer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1200835-does-the-half-life-merit-really-turn-you-into-a-vampire-wraith-hybrid?p=1201357#post1201357\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I don't consider the Merit overpowered at all.<br /> <br /> But I wrote it, so I would say that <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>Hi, as the writer can you explain how the merit actually mechanically works.<br /> <br /> Do you only get the dots 2-5 of secondary path for half the price, or also the also the ones for your primary path/the Discipline.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5199-aahz","name":"Aahz","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"610"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-30T15:30:49-07:00","id":1201437,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Gentleman Gamer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1200835-does-the-half-life-merit-really-turn-you-into-a-vampire-wraith-hybrid?p=1201357#post1201357\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I don't consider the Merit overpowered at all.<br /> <br /> But I wrote it, so I would say that <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>So it does grant access to all Wraith abilities and powers, then?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12085-beriorn","name":"Beriorn","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12085_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-30T15:36:19-07:00","id":1201442,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aahz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1200835-does-the-half-life-merit-really-turn-you-into-a-vampire-wraith-hybrid?p=1201407#post1201407\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Hi, as the writer can you explain how the merit actually mechanically works.<br /> <br /> Do you only get the dots 2-5 of secondary path for half the price, or also the also the ones for your primary path/the Discipline.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>Is it ambiguous? It says Path, not Discipline. When you raise your Necromancy trait, you're increasing a Discipline in terms of EXP expenditure.<br /> <br /> So I read it as dots 2-5 of all of your Secondary paths.<br /> <br /> And on top of that the thing where you can teleport between the two sides of the Shroud with no roll, independent of the thickness of the shroud. Pretty potent!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11620-twig","name":"twig","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11620_5.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4568"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-30T16:40:20-07:00","id":1201462,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kammerer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1200835-does-the-half-life-merit-really-turn-you-into-a-vampire-wraith-hybrid?p=1201206#post1201206\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Well as written the merit has no unforseen consequences. It's weird and it raises more questions than it answers, but it has no consequences.</div> </div> </div> </div>If at any point during the day today, you heard a loud whizzing sound above you, it was <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Half-Life_(video_game)\" target=\"_blank\">the joke</a>.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/431-theodrim","name":"Theodrim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar431_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1841"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-31T12:19:47-07:00","id":1201678,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Beriorn</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1200835-does-the-half-life-merit-really-turn-you-into-a-vampire-wraith-hybrid?p=1201437#post1201437\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So it does grant access to all Wraith abilities and powers, then?</div> </div> </div> </div>No, and the Merit doesn't say you do. The benefits are:<br /> <br /> - You only spend half the regular experience points for increasing Necromancy Paths after you've purchased the first dot on the Path.<br /> - You can move between Skinlands and Shadowlands by spending a Willpower point.<br /> - You have two auras: one for the vampire, one for the wraith.<br /> <br /> Kindred hunt you mercilessly if they find out you're not a true vampire for a few reasons:<br /> <br /> - You're an oddity ripe for study.<br /> - They want to know if you're one of many unusual vampires in Kindred society.<br /> - Necromancers see you as a threat.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><span style=\"color:#000080\">Matthew Dawkins</span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000080\">In-House Developer for Onyx Path Publishing</span></b><br /> <br /> <i><span style=\"font-family:arial\"><b><span style=\"color:#008080\">Website: </span><a href=\"http://www.matthewdawkins.com\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008080\">https://www.matthewdawkins.com</span></a><br /> <span style=\"color:#008080\">Patreon: </span><a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/matthewdawkins\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008080\">https://www.patreon.com/matthewdawkins</span></a></b></span></i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/152-the-gentleman-gamer","name":"The Gentleman Gamer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar152_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1698"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-31T15:52:30-07:00","id":1201728,"title":"","content":"So what about using the Merit for Vampires who have their soul removed with Necromancy and a Wraith placed into them? Most subjects probably won't know necromancy, but the merit is more for flavor on my part.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/754-eldagusto","name":"Eldagusto","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar754_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-02T15:14:56-07:00","id":1202314,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Eldagusto</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1200835-does-the-half-life-merit-really-turn-you-into-a-vampire-wraith-hybrid?p=1201728#post1201728\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So what about using the Merit for Vampires who have their soul removed with Necromancy and a Wraith placed into them? Most subjects probably won't know necromancy, but the merit is more for flavor on my part.</div> </div> </div> </div>Bone Path can, with a lot of successes and good timing, put a Wraith inside the body of a Kindred who was just Diablerized immediately before. I'd happily grant that merit to the resulting creation, and honestly I feel like &quot;I'm a Wraith in a Vampire's Body&quot; is a great excuse to just immediately have Necromancy as an Additional Discipline. Ash 1 makes a lot of sense for a Wraith who has just been trapped in a Cainite shell.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11620-twig","name":"twig","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11620_5.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4568"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-09-30T14:42:14-07:00","id":1523371,"title":"","content":"<br /> <b><i>Thread Necromancy on a thread about... Necromancy.</i></b><br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> I have asked lots of questions about the V20 Necromancy merits and powers. But now I am seeing this thread for the first time.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>11twiggins</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1200835-does-the-half-life-merit-really-turn-you-into-a-vampire-wraith-hybrid?p=1201319#post1201319\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <b>Except to have Half-Life you need to be a Cainite who has spent a long time in the Shadowlands, and to be a Mortuario you need to have undergone a ritual only the premascine Giovanni (those who were embraced before the Cappadocian betrayal) have.</b><br /> <br /> Yes it is entirely mechanically plausible to be a Mortuario Harbinger with Half-Life, but no ST is going to okay that. Furthermore, you've wasted the vast majority of your freebies, so you are EXTREMELY GOOD at the 1-3 dots of one path of Necromancy you have.<br /> <br /> These two merits require a deeply contorted backstory which no one will okay.<b> I died accidentally, and a Harbinger and a Premascine worked together to bring me back</b>, and then kicked me into torpor in the shadowlands for 100 years... NO! I am NOT powergaming!</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I have seen many merits in the &quot;Lore of Bloodlines/Clans&quot; that are Clan restrictive, but some are open for anyone or for large number of Kindred. <b>Half-Life</b> does not seem to imply that a Harbinger need to be involved, and the <b>Mortuario </b>merit itself provides good backstory for <b>Half-Life</b> (the ritual that brings you back is calling your wraith).<br /> <br /> <br /> Some of the open merits/flaws are the Tzimisce &quot;<b>Bioluminescence</b>&quot;, <b>&quot;Pain Tolerance</b>&quot;, &quot;<b>Promethean Clay</b>&quot; (2 only require to have Vissicitude); Tremere &quot;<b>Arcane Curse</b>&quot; &quot;<b>Mage Blood</b>&quot;; Lasombra &quot;<b>Aura of Command</b>&quot;. Nothing in those merits makes them Clan specific, unlike &quot;<b>Thaumaturgically Inept</b>&quot; (Only Tremere can take this Flaw) or &quot;<b>Blessed by St. Gustav</b>&quot; (Only Ventrue antitribu can take this Merit).<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> \u200b<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":4967,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4967-lbeaumanior","user":"lbeaumanior","date":". 04-09-2024, 11:00 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4967-lbeaumanior","name":"lbeaumanior","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4967_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-10-03T20:03:57-07:00","id":1523523,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Bluecho</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1200835-does-the-half-life-merit-really-turn-you-into-a-vampire-wraith-hybrid?p=1201180#post1201180\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">As stated earlier, this Merit doesn't imply in the least that the character can learn Arcanoi, have the benefits of Lifesight or Deathsight, or any other aspect of the Wraith condition. If that had been the intent, the designers would have spelled that out directly in the Merit itself, as they spelled out the mechanics being a Ghoul over in Mage.<br /> <br /> <br /> This, however, is not why I'm here. I'm here to ask: If the Merit DID allow the Vampire to learn Arcanoi, would be actually be overpowered, as the original poster said?<br /> <br /> I don't think so. Setting aside for a moment that many Arcanoi may not even be applicable for a Vampire (I'm not familiar enough with Wraith to say either way). Or how of all the powers available to the Vampires, I can't imagine any Arcanoi would be very much more powerful than some of the Disciplines VtM has created over the years. Let's not even mention these points.<br /> <br /> Instead, here's this. There's a school of thought that says if you give one supernatural creature access to two different sets of powers, that also means the character must DIVIDE their experience points between the two powers. Even if the breadth of abilities a character could access is huge, their ability to learn and improve them is finite. If continuing to gain new and different powers is, in and of itself, inherently OP, then what makes a Vampire learning Arcanoi qualitatively different than learning out-of-clan Disciplines? Or blood sorcery, with its many Paths and Rituals?<br /> <br /> All for powers that are, at least in theory, as good as powers they gain natively, if dot ranks are anything to go by?<br /> <br /> The only possible exception to this tends to be Mage Spheres, since their applications are open-ended and flexible in a way other supernatural powers aren't. But even then, you're also investing large amounts of experience into those Spheres, AND into Arete, AND into any number of mundane Abilities that the character's Focus may rely upon to channel Effects. AND the use of those Sphere powers is subject to Paradox, which puts a ceiling on the kinds of things our hypothetical cross-trained supernatural creature can use &quot;safely&quot;.<br /> <br /> Not to mention, whether you're a different splat branching INTO Spheres or a Mage branching OUT, many of the powers gained (that you just spent a bunch of experience unlocking) will be redundant to powers you already have. But I digress.<br /> <br /> <br /> My point is, while I'd personally be reluctant to allow different splats free rein to learn each others' powers, I'm skeptical that allowing it would really break the game. On paper, letting Vampires learn Arcanoi SOUNDS overpowered. But in practice, the character is, at best, edging out advantages at unexpected angles, at the cost of failing to refine the greatest of their own native powers. Not useless, no, but neither is it a path to overwhelming power.</div> </div> </div> </div>Actually Risen has access to both Arcanoi and some Disciplines and nobody ever thought of them as broken.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27429-microcuchon","name":"Microcuchon","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"201"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}